course: dictionary
lesson: 10064
title: What is a text?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A text is written words. It can be in a book, on a screen, or on paper. In class, a text is a piece of writing you read and study, such as a story, a poem, an article or a set of instructions.
explain: Texts can be fiction, which is a made-up story, or non-fiction, which is true writing such as a report about animals. When your teacher says «find evidence in the text», look back at the words on the page and find the sentence that proves your answer.
explain: The word text has another meaning. A text message is a short written message sent from one phone to another, and to text someone means to send them one. «Text speak» shortens words, so c means see, u means you and l8r means later.
explain: «You do not need to reread the whole text for every question.» Read the question first, then find the part of the text that answers it.
fact: A text is any piece of writing you read, such as a story, poem, article or set of instructions.
fact: «Text speak» shortens words with letters and numbers that sound like them: c (see), u (you), l8r (later), m8 (mate).
fact: «Phishing» means tricking someone into giving private details, like a login or card number.
fact: Scam texts about parcels, prizes and unpaid bills trick many people every year into giving away card details.
fact: Only text people you know in real life, and tell an adult if a text upsets you.
exercise: In class, what is a text? | A picture with no words | *A piece of writing you read, like a story or an article | A type of football pitch | A loud noise made by a phone
exercise: In text speak, what does «c» mean? | cut | cat | can | *see
exercise: A text says you have won a prize and must send your card number now. What should you do? | Send the card number quickly before the prize goes | Send it to all your friends so they can win too | Text back with your address and birthday | *Do not reply, and tell an adult
test: «You do not need to reread the whole text for every question.» What does this tell you? | You should never read a text at all | *You can look only at the part of the text that answers the question | You can guess every answer | You must read every word again for each question
test: «Phishing» means what? | Sending a long text message to a friend | *Tricking someone into giving away private details, like a login | Reading a book aloud | Fishing with a phone
exam: What is it called when you copy text and pass it off as your own? | A text message | *Plagiarism, a kind of cheating | Good writing | Phishing
